## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Install the following tools:

- Node.js
- npm
- MySQL
- Git

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Sbh-01/home-supervision.git
```

### 2. Navigate to the Project

```bash
cd home-supervision
```

### 3. Set Up the Backend

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

### 4. Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the backend directory.

```env
PORT=5000
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=your_database_user
DB_PASSWORD=your_database_password
DB_NAME=home_supervision
```

Use your own local database credentials. Never commit your `.env` file.

### 5. Set Up the Database

Configure Prisma and your database connection, then run the appropriate migration command for your project.

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev
npx prisma generate
```

### 6. Start the Backend

```bash
npm run dev
```

The backend will run at:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

### 7. Start the Frontend

Open another terminal:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm start
```

Use the frontend start command configured in your `package.json`. If your project uses a different script, adjust the command accordingly.

